    "seed": 20260923,
    "what_follows_by_reading": [
      "The 48 shared tensors are drawn before the head, from the same generator states as with the switch OFF.",
      "After the container is built, the CPU generator is back in the state it had before the head, so later CPU draws are the same as with the switch OFF.",
      "The head does not touch the CUDA generator, so CUDA draws are not moved either.",
      "Between Helm 2.0 source 20208c92 and ceab6c49, pointer_learner.py changed the container only by appending the head, two argument checks, read-only switch properties and comments. No shared tensor was reordered or re-initialised (read from git diff 20208c92..ceab6c49)."
    ],
    "what_the_code_does": [
      "The analogy head is built LAST, after every one of the 48 shared tensors.",
      "It is built inside torch.random.fork_rng(devices=[]), which saves the CPU generator state first and restores it afterwards.",
      "Inside that block the CPU generator is seeded with analogy_seed (20260923); the head's Linear layers draw their initial values on the CPU, then move to the device. LayerNorm starts at ones and zeros.",
      "devices=[] means no CUDA generator is saved, reseeded or used by the head."
    ]
  },
